+/* GIMP - The GNU Image Manipulation Program
+ * Copyright (C) 1995 Spencer Kimball and Peter Mattis
+ *
+ * chopgimp-brushes-panel.c — ChopGimp 3.30.0 (bloc vectoriel 4): the
+ * « Formes » dockable, Illustrator's Brushes panel
+ *
+ *    ▭ Calligraphique 1        (one row per brush of the library: a
+ *    ▭ Art 2                    preview of its artwork, its name)
+ *    Nouvelle : [Art ▾]   Tuile : [Côté ▾]
+ *    [+] [⇣] [✎] [▦] [⎘] [Aa] [🗑]
+ *
+ *  - Nouvelle forme: a brush of the chosen type (artwork: the selected
+ *    objects, else the built-in one);
+ *  - Appliquer (or a double-click): the selected paths take it;
+ *  - Modifier: its options; the brushed paths of the image follow;
+ *  - Tuile: the selected objects become the chosen tile of a pattern
+ *    brush (side, outer / inner corner, start, end);
+ *  - Dupliquer, Renommer, Supprimer (brushed paths keep their look).
+ *
+ * The library is kept in <gimpdir>/chopgimp-brushes and in the images
+ * (merged into the library when the panel sees the image).
